<template><div class="page"><div class="site-container prose"><span class="eyebrow">Security</span><h1>Report vulnerabilities responsibly.</h1><p>Do not open a public issue for an unpatched vulnerability. Use the private security advisory channel in the GitHub repository after it is created.</p><h2>Supply chain</h2><ul><li>Public packages contain only declared distribution files.</li><li>CI builds and tests every release.</li><li>npm provenance is required for official publication.</li><li>Long-lived npm tokens are avoided through trusted publishing.</li></ul><h2>Supported versions</h2><p>Before 1.0, security fixes target the latest alpha or beta. Stable support windows will be published with 1.0.</p></div></div></template>
